<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Burmese Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1824–1885</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Burmese Wars were three wars fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> and the Konbaung kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in the nineteenth century. The First (1824–1826) cost Burma Arakan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanintharyi-region">Tenasserim</a> and its claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> and Manipur; the Second (1852–1853) gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a>; and the Third (1885) ended the monarchy, after which all of Burma was annexed to British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-burmese-wars.jpg" alt="Anglo-Burmese Wars" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willoughby Wallace Hooper · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Third_anglo-burmese_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
